Subject: [PATCH] tcp_buf: record the connection of flag-only frames

tcp_buf_send_flag() queues SYN/ACK/FIN frames (and the DUP_ACK copy)
without setting tcp_frame_conns[] for them; only the data path does. If
tap_send_frames() then fails, for example because no guest is attached
to the socket yet, tcp_payload_flush() calls tcp_revert_seq() on those
frames with a NULL or stale connection pointer and passt crashes
(SEGV in tcp_revert_seq) or rewinds another connection's sequence.

qrab hits it when inbound TCP reaches a NIC pod's stable address while
QEMU has not reconnected yet (work/passt-flag-frame-revert-crash).
---
--- a/tcp_buf.c
+++ b/tcp_buf.c
@@ -209,13 +209,18 @@
 	if (ret <= 0)
 		return ret;
 
+	/* tcp_revert_seq() needs the owner of every queued frame */
+	tcp_frame_conns[tcp_payload_used] = conn;
 	tcp_payload_used++;
 	l4len = optlen + sizeof(struct tcphdr);
 	iov[TCP_IOV_PAYLOAD].iov_len = l4len;
 	tcp_l2_buf_fill_headers(conn, iov, NULL, seq, false);
 
 	if (flags & DUP_ACK) {
-		struct iovec *dup_iov = tcp_l2_iov[tcp_payload_used++];
+		struct iovec *dup_iov;
+
+		tcp_frame_conns[tcp_payload_used] = conn;
+		dup_iov = tcp_l2_iov[tcp_payload_used++];
 
 		memcpy(dup_iov[TCP_IOV_TAP].iov_base, iov[TCP_IOV_TAP].iov_base,
 		       iov[TCP_IOV_TAP].iov_len);
